    ],
    "summary": "I couldn't build five drawers in a single hex base: the configurator only allows one. Drawers sit on the cut face of a half base, and a half base has just one cut face. A full base has none, so I swapped the full base for a north half base (piece:0,0,0;half-n). It takes exactly one drawer, which I added (drawer:0#0,0#cut). When I asked for more spots after that, there were none. The only way to get more drawers is to add more bases beside or on top, and the brief rules that out. I also left off the end caps and joint bolts to keep to \"nothing else added\". The check passes with no rule errors and the mesh-collision check reads clear.",
